IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lta-assurance-fund`

-- Land Titles Act 1993, Part 17 -- worked cases.
--
-- Claims about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The running
-- example is the one the Torrens system is built around: a forger registers a
-- transfer of someone else's land and sells it on to a buyer who knows nothing.

§ `Fixtures -- proprietors`

GIVEN `is proprietor` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `party to the fraud` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `agent party to it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `predecessor acted in bad faith` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a purchaser` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `known disability` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `unlawful statutory acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `party to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a trustee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Proprietor
DECIDE `a proprietor` `is proprietor` `party to the fraud` `agent party to it` `predecessor acted in bad faith` `a purchaser` `known disability` `unlawful statutory acquisition` `party to the contract` `a trustee` IS
    Proprietor WITH
        `became the proprietor of registered land` IS `is proprietor`
        `was a party to, or colluded in, the fraud or forgery` IS `party to the fraud`
        `the proprietor's agent was a party to or colluded in it` IS `agent party to it`
        `a predecessor in title acted in bad faith` IS `predecessor acted in bad faith`
        `claims as a purchaser` IS `a purchaser`
        `acquired the land from a person under a known legal disability` IS `known disability`
        `unlawfully acquired the land in purported exercise of a statutory power` IS `unlawful statutory acquisition`
        `was a party to the contract sought to be enforced` IS `party to the contract`
        `is a trustee of the land` IS `a trustee`

`the forger, now registered` MEANS `a proprietor` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`the innocent buyer from the forger` MEANS `a proprietor` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`the forger's relative, who was given the land` MEANS `a proprietor` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`a buyer whose own agent was in on the forgery` MEANS `a proprietor` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an authority that acquired the land under an invalid statutory power` MEANS `a proprietor` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a proprietor who is a trustee` MEANS `a proprietor` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
`an ordinary proprietor with nothing against them` MEANS `a proprietor` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `Fixtures -- actions for the recovery of land`

GIVEN `mortgagee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `chargee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `lessor` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `deprived by fraud` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `unlawfully acquired` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `defendant registered by fraud` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `defendant a volunteer through the fraudster` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `re-entry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A RecoveryAction
DECIDE `a recovery action` `mortgagee` `chargee` `lessor` `deprived by fraud` `unlawfully acquired` `defendant registered by fraud` `defendant a volunteer through the fraudster` `re-entry` IS
    RecoveryAction WITH
        `a mortgagee against a mortgagor in default` IS `mortgagee`
        `a chargee against a chargor in default` IS `chargee`
        `a lessor against a lessee in default` IS `lessor`
        `the claimant was deprived of land by fraud` IS `deprived by fraud`
        `the land was unlawfully acquired, whether or not under purported statutory authority` IS `unlawfully acquired`
        `the defendant became registered as proprietor by fraud` IS `defendant registered by fraud`
        `the defendant claims through that proprietor otherwise than as a purchaser` IS `defendant a volunteer through the fraudster`
        `a re-entry or forfeiture on breach of a State title covenant` IS `re-entry`

`the dispossessed owner against the forger` MEANS `a recovery action` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`the dispossessed owner against the forger's donee` MEANS `a recovery action` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
`the dispossessed owner against the innocent buyer` MEANS `a recovery action` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
`an owner against an authority that acquired unlawfully` MEANS `a recovery action` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
`a mortgagee against a defaulting mortgagor` MEANS `a recovery action` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `Fixtures -- the Registrar's conduct`

GIVEN `electronic` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `something went wrong` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it was the particulars` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in registration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A RegistrarsConduct
DECIDE `conduct` `electronic` `something went wrong` `it was the particulars` `in registration` IS
    RegistrarsConduct WITH
        `the instrument was lodged in electronic form under section 51A` IS `electronic`
        `the Registrar omitted something, made a mistake, or committed a misfeasance` IS `something went wrong`
        `what went wrong was an inaccuracy in the particulars as lodged` IS `it was the particulars`
        `it occurred in bringing the land under this Act or in registering an instrument` IS `in registration`

-- A paper lodgment the Registrar registered against the wrong folio.
`a paper lodgment registered against the wrong folio` MEANS `conduct` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
-- An electronic lodgment whose particulars were wrong, which the Registrar
-- registered exactly as lodged.
`an electronic lodgment with wrong particulars, registered as lodged` MEANS `conduct` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- The same inaccuracy on a paper lodgment, where the Registrar still had the duty
-- to inquire.
`a paper lodgment with wrong particulars` MEANS `conduct` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- A clean forgery the Registrar handled correctly: nothing went wrong at the
-- Registry at all.
`a clean forgery, correctly registered` MEANS `conduct` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE

§ `Fixtures -- fund claims`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A RegistrarsConduct,
      `what went wrong` IS A WhatWentWrong,
      `deprived` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `may sue someone else` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `own neglect contributed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `withheld entirely` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `years since` IS A NUMBER,
      `earlier action discontinued` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `years since discontinuance` IS A NUMBER,
      `notice served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A FundClaim
DECIDE `a fund claim` `the conduct` `what went wrong` `deprived` `may sue someone else` `own neglect contributed` `withheld entirely` `years since` `earlier action discontinued` `years since discontinuance` `notice served` IS
    FundClaim WITH
        `the Registrar's conduct` IS `the conduct`
        `what went wrong` IS `what went wrong`
        `the claimant was deprived of land or sustained loss or damage` IS `deprived`
        `the claimant may bring an action for the recovery of the land, the proceeds of sale, mortgage moneys or a caveated interest` IS `may sue someone else`
        `the claimant's own neglect, default or incaution contributed` IS `own neglect contributed`
        `the court has decided to withhold compensation altogether for that reason` IS `withheld entirely`
        `years since the deprivation occurred or the loss was sustained` IS `years since`
        `an earlier action for the same cause was discontinued` IS `earlier action discontinued`
        `years since that discontinuance` IS `years since discontinuance`
        `notice of the claim was served on the Registrar at least 14 days before commencement` IS `notice served`

-- The claim that works: the Registrar's own error on a paper lodgment, the owner
-- barred against everyone, within time, notice given.
`a good claim on a Registry error` MEANS
    `a fund claim` `a paper lodgment registered against the wrong folio` `something else` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 3 FALSE 0 TRUE

-- The same, but the owner can still sue the forger for the proceeds of sale.
`the same claim, where the forger can still be sued` MEANS
    `a fund claim` `a paper lodgment registered against the wrong folio` `something else` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 3 FALSE 0 TRUE

-- A clean forgery, correctly registered: the owner has lost everything and the
-- Registrar did nothing wrong.
`a clean forgery, the owner barred against the buyer` MEANS
    `a fund claim` `a clean forgery, correctly registered` `something else` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 3 FALSE 0 TRUE

-- The electronic-lodgment case: the particulars were wrong and the Registrar was
-- obliged to register them as lodged.
`wrong particulars on an electronic lodgment` MEANS
    `a fund claim` `an electronic lodgment with wrong particulars, registered as lodged` `something else` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 3 FALSE 0 TRUE

-- The identical inaccuracy on a paper lodgment.
`the same wrong particulars on paper` MEANS
    `a fund claim` `a paper lodgment with wrong particulars` `something else` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 3 FALSE 0 TRUE

-- The s 155(3) exclusions.
`a boundary mis-description from the Chief Surveyor` MEANS
    `a fund claim` `a paper lodgment registered against the wrong folio` `an incorrect description of the parcels, boundaries or dimensions from the Chief Surveyor` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 3 FALSE 0 TRUE
`a qualified folio` MEANS
    `a fund claim` `a paper lodgment registered against the wrong folio` `the issue of a qualified folio` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 3 FALSE 0 TRUE
`a dimension error where no survey was carried out` MEANS
    `a fund claim` `a paper lodgment registered against the wrong folio` `an incorrect or absent description of parcels or dimensions where no survey was carried out` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 3 FALSE 0 TRUE
`a trustee proprietor's breach of trust` MEANS
    `a fund claim` `a paper lodgment registered against the wrong folio` `a breach by a proprietor of a trust` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 3 FALSE 0 TRUE

-- Limitation.
`a good claim, twelve years on` MEANS
    `a fund claim` `a paper lodgment registered against the wrong folio` `something else` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 12 FALSE 0 TRUE
`a good claim, thirteen years on` MEANS
    `a fund claim` `a paper lodgment registered against the wrong folio` `something else` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 13 FALSE 0 TRUE
`thirteen years on, after a discontinuance last year` MEANS
    `a fund claim` `a paper lodgment registered against the wrong folio` `something else` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 13 TRUE 1 TRUE
`thirteen years on, after a discontinuance three years ago` MEANS
    `a fund claim` `a paper lodgment registered against the wrong folio` `something else` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 13 TRUE 3 TRUE
-- The claimant who fought the forger to judgment and lost, and is now out of
-- time. s 158(2) names discontinuance and nothing else.
`thirteen years on, after losing the action against the forger` MEANS
    `a fund claim` `a paper lodgment registered against the wrong folio` `something else` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 13 FALSE 0 TRUE

-- Notice, and contributory neglect.
`a good claim with no notice served` MEANS
    `a fund claim` `a paper lodgment registered against the wrong folio` `something else` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 3 FALSE 0 FALSE
`a good claim where the claimant was careless` MEANS
    `a fund claim` `a paper lodgment registered against the wrong folio` `something else` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 3 FALSE 0 TRUE
`a good claim where the court withheld compensation entirely` MEANS
    `a fund claim` `a paper lodgment registered against the wrong folio` `something else` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 3 FALSE 0 TRUE

§ `Section 46 and section 157 -- the register protects the buyer`

-- The forger does not get the benefit of indefeasibility: s 46(2)(a).
#ASSERT `a limb of section 46(2) is made out against this proprietor` `the forger, now registered`
#ASSERT NOT `the proprietor's title is indefeasible against the dispossessed owner` `the forger, now registered`

-- The innocent buyer does, "despite any lack of good faith on the part of the
-- person through whom that person claims".
#ASSERT NOT `a limb of section 46(2) is made out against this proprietor` `the innocent buyer from the forger`
#ASSERT `the proprietor's title is indefeasible against the dispossessed owner` `the innocent buyer from the forger`
#ASSERT `section 157(1) bars an action against this proprietor for the land or the money` `the innocent buyer from the forger`

-- s 46(3): a volunteer does not. The forger's gift to a relative is reachable
-- where the forger's sale to a buyer is not.
#ASSERT `section 46(3) leaves this proprietor exposed to the predecessor's defect` `the forger's relative, who was given the land`
#ASSERT NOT `the proprietor's title is indefeasible against the dispossessed owner` `the forger's relative, who was given the land`
#ASSERT NOT `section 157(1) bars an action against this proprietor for the land or the money` `the forger's relative, who was given the land`

-- And a buyer whose own agent was in on it is outside the protection: s 46(2)(a)
-- names the proprietor's agent.
#ASSERT `a limb of section 46(2) is made out against this proprietor` `a buyer whose own agent was in on the forgery`
#ASSERT NOT `the proprietor's title is indefeasible against the dispossessed owner` `a buyer whose own agent was in on the forgery`
#ASSERT NOT `section 157(1) bars an action against this proprietor for the land or the money` `a buyer whose own agent was in on the forgery`

-- The other s 46(2) limbs.
#ASSERT `a limb of section 46(2) is made out against this proprietor` `an authority that acquired the land under an invalid statutory power`
#ASSERT `a limb of section 46(2) is made out against this proprietor` `a proprietor who is a trustee`
#ASSERT `the proprietor's title is indefeasible against the dispossessed owner` `an ordinary proprietor with nothing against them`

-- s 157(2) protects the official personally and says nothing about the fund.
#ASSERT `section 157(2) protects the official personally` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `section 157(2) protects the official personally` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar's good faith is an answer to a claim against the fund`

§ `Section 154 -- which proprietary actions survive`

#ASSERT `section 154(1)(d) permits the action` `the dispossessed owner against the forger`
#ASSERT `an action for the recovery of registered land lies` `the dispossessed owner against the forger`

-- "Or against any person claiming through that proprietor otherwise than as a
-- purchaser": the donee is reachable.
#ASSERT `section 154(1)(d) permits the action` `the dispossessed owner against the forger's donee`
#ASSERT `an action for the recovery of registered land lies` `the dispossessed owner against the forger's donee`

-- The innocent buyer is not.
#ASSERT NOT `section 154(1)(d) permits the action` `the dispossessed owner against the innocent buyer`
#ASSERT NOT `an action for the recovery of registered land lies` `the dispossessed owner against the innocent buyer`

-- s 154(5) deems an unlawful acquisition fraudulent, so limb (d) reaches an
-- authority that acquired under an invalid power without anyone proving
-- dishonesty.
#ASSERT `there was a deprivation by fraud for the purposes of section 154` `an owner against an authority that acquired unlawfully`
#ASSERT NOT `an owner against an authority that acquired unlawfully`'s `the claimant was deprived of land by fraud`
#ASSERT `an action for the recovery of registered land lies` `an owner against an authority that acquired unlawfully`

#ASSERT `an action for the recovery of registered land lies` `a mortgagee against a defaulting mortgagor`

§ `Section 155 -- the first element is the Registrar, not the register`

-- THE THING A LAYPERSON WILL GET WRONG. The assurance fund does not insure the
-- effect of the register; it insures the Registrar's conduct. A clean forgery
-- that the Registry handled correctly gives no claim at all, however complete
-- the owner's loss.
#ASSERT NOT `an omission, mistake or misfeasance of the Registrar is established` `a clean forgery, correctly registered`
#ASSERT `a clean forgery, the owner barred against the buyer`'s `the claimant was deprived of land or sustained loss or damage`
#ASSERT NOT `an action against the assurance fund lies` `a clean forgery, the owner barred against the buyer`

-- Where the Registrar did get something wrong, the claim lies.
#ASSERT `an omission, mistake or misfeasance of the Registrar is established` `a paper lodgment registered against the wrong folio`
#ASSERT `an action against the assurance fund lies` `a good claim on a Registry error`
#ASSERT `the claimant recovers something from the fund` `a good claim on a Registry error`

§ `Section 51A(4) -- the electronic lodgment that nobody had to check`

-- s 51A(4)(b) relieves the Registrar of the duty to inquire into the accuracy of
-- the particulars on an electronic lodgment and obliges registration in
-- accordance with them. s 155(1) needs an omission or mistake of the Registrar.
#ASSERT `the Registrar bore a duty to inquire into the accuracy of the particulars` `a paper lodgment with wrong particulars`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar bore a duty to inquire into the accuracy of the particulars` `an electronic lodgment with wrong particulars, registered as lodged`

-- THE SAME INACCURACY, AND A DIFFERENT ANSWER, DEPENDING ONLY ON THE FORM OF
-- LODGMENT.
#ASSERT `an omission, mistake or misfeasance of the Registrar is established` `a paper lodgment with wrong particulars`
#ASSERT NOT `an omission, mistake or misfeasance of the Registrar is established` `an electronic lodgment with wrong particulars, registered as lodged`
#ASSERT `an action against the assurance fund lies` `the same wrong particulars on paper`
#ASSERT NOT `an action against the assurance fund lies` `wrong particulars on an electronic lodgment`

§ `Section 155(4) -- the deeming that sends the claimant away`

-- s 155(4) does not merely withhold the fund claim from a person with another
-- remedy. It deems them to have suffered NO LOSS AT ALL.
#ASSERT `section 155(4) deems the claimant to have suffered no loss` `the same claim, where the forger can still be sued`
#ASSERT NOT `the claimant is barred from an action for recovery as section 155(1) requires` `the same claim, where the forger can still be sued`
#ASSERT NOT `an action against the assurance fund lies` `the same claim, where the forger can still be sued`

-- Identical facts, except that the forger has gone beyond reach.
#ASSERT NOT `section 155(4) deems the claimant to have suffered no loss` `a good claim on a Registry error`
#ASSERT `an action against the assurance fund lies` `a good claim on a Registry error`

§ `Sections 155(3) and 151(5) -- what the fund never pays for`

-- "Under any circumstances", so the Registrar's own fault does not bring it back:
-- each of these fixtures has a proved Registry error and still fails.
#ASSERT `an omission, mistake or misfeasance of the Registrar is established` (`a boundary mis-description from the Chief Surveyor`'s `the Registrar's conduct`)
#ASSERT `section 155(3) excludes compensation` `an incorrect description of the parcels, boundaries or dimensions from the Chief Surveyor`
#ASSERT NOT `an action against the assurance fund lies` `a boundary mis-description from the Chief Surveyor`

#ASSERT `section 155(3) excludes compensation` `the issue of a qualified folio`
#ASSERT NOT `an action against the assurance fund lies` `a qualified folio`
#ASSERT `section 155(3) excludes compensation` `an incorrect or absent description of parcels or dimensions where no survey was carried out`
#ASSERT NOT `an action against the assurance fund lies` `a dimension error where no survey was carried out`

-- s 151(5): and never for a proprietor's breach of trust.
#ASSERT `section 151(5) excludes compensation` `a breach by a proprietor of a trust`
#ASSERT NOT `an action against the assurance fund lies` `a trustee proprietor's breach of trust`

#ASSERT NOT `section 155(3) excludes compensation` `something else`
#ASSERT NOT `section 151(5) excludes compensation` `something else`

§ `Section 158 -- twelve years from the error, and one way to extend it`

#ASSERT `the claim is within the twelve years in section 158(1)` `a good claim, twelve years on`
#ASSERT `an action against the assurance fund lies` `a good claim, twelve years on`
#ASSERT NOT `the claim is within the twelve years in section 158(1)` `a good claim, thirteen years on`
#ASSERT NOT `an action against the assurance fund lies` `a good claim, thirteen years on`

-- s 158(2): one year after the DISCONTINUANCE of the earlier action.
#ASSERT `section 158(2) extends the time` `thirteen years on, after a discontinuance last year`
#ASSERT `the claim is in time` `thirteen years on, after a discontinuance last year`
#ASSERT `an action against the assurance fund lies` `thirteen years on, after a discontinuance last year`
#ASSERT NOT `section 158(2) extends the time` `thirteen years on, after a discontinuance three years ago`
#ASSERT NOT `an action against the assurance fund lies` `thirteen years on, after a discontinuance three years ago`

-- AND NOTHING ELSE. The claimant who fought the forger to judgment and lost gets
-- no extra year, although s 155(4) is what obliged them to bring that action in
-- the first place.
#ASSERT NOT `section 158(2) extends the time` `thirteen years on, after losing the action against the forger`
#ASSERT NOT `an action against the assurance fund lies` `thirteen years on, after losing the action against the forger`

§ `Sections 155(2) and 156(1) -- notice, and the claimant's own carelessness`

-- s 156(1): fourteen days' notice to the Registrar as nominal defendant.
#ASSERT NOT `an action against the assurance fund lies` `a good claim with no notice served`

-- s 155(2): the court "may withhold or abate" for the claimant's own neglect, so
-- contributory fault can defeat the claim entirely rather than reduce it.
#ASSERT `the court may withhold or abate the compensation` `a good claim where the claimant was careless`
#ASSERT `an action against the assurance fund lies` `a good claim where the claimant was careless`
#ASSERT `the claimant recovers something from the fund` `a good claim where the claimant was careless`
#ASSERT `an action against the assurance fund lies` `a good claim where the court withheld compensation entirely`
#ASSERT NOT `the claimant recovers something from the fund` `a good claim where the court withheld compensation entirely`
#ASSERT NOT `the court may withhold or abate the compensation` `a good claim on a Registry error`

§ `Sections 155(6) and (7) -- an offer, not an acceptance`

#ASSERT `further action is limited to determining the compensation` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `further action is limited to determining the compensation` FALSE

-- s 155(7) attaches to the MAKING of the offer. Nothing requires the claimant to
-- accept it or the amount to be adequate.
#ASSERT NOT `the claimant must accept the offer for section 155(7) to bite`

§ `Section 156(2) -- the twenty per cent rule`

GIVEN `tendered` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `amount` IS A NUMBER,
      `rejected` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `recovered` IS A NUMBER,
      `final judgment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Tender
DECIDE `a tender` `tendered` `amount` `rejected` `recovered` `final judgment` IS
    Tender WITH
        `the Registrar tendered an amount` IS `tendered`
        `the amount tendered, in dollars` IS `amount`
        `the claimant rejected the tender` IS `rejected`
        `the damages recovered, in dollars` IS `recovered`
        `the claimant recovered final judgment against the Registrar` IS `final judgment`

`rejected $100,000 and recovered $115,000` MEANS `a tender` TRUE 100000 TRUE 115000 TRUE
`rejected $100,000 and recovered $120,000` MEANS `a tender` TRUE 100000 TRUE 120000 TRUE
`rejected $100,000 and recovered $130,000` MEANS `a tender` TRUE 100000 TRUE 130000 TRUE
`rejected $100,000 and recovered $90,000` MEANS `a tender` TRUE 100000 TRUE 90000 TRUE
`accepted the tender` MEANS `a tender` TRUE 100000 FALSE 100000 FALSE
`no tender, final judgment for $50,000` MEANS `a tender` FALSE 0 FALSE 50000 TRUE
`no tender, and the claim was settled` MEANS `a tender` FALSE 0 FALSE 50000 FALSE

#ASSERT `the figure the claimant must exceed under section 156(2)` `rejected $100,000 and recovered $115,000` EQUALS 120000

-- The claimant must beat the tender by MORE THAN a fifth, not merely beat it.
-- $115,000 against a $100,000 tender is a win on the action and a loss on costs.
#ASSERT NOT `the claimant beat the tender by enough` `rejected $100,000 and recovered $115,000`
#ASSERT `section 156(2) makes the claimant pay the Registrar's costs` `rejected $100,000 and recovered $115,000`
#ASSERT NOT `the fund bears the claimant's costs` `rejected $100,000 and recovered $115,000`
#ASSERT `the claimant pays the Registrar's costs` `rejected $100,000 and recovered $115,000`

-- Exactly 20% more is not "exceeding ... by 20%".
#ASSERT NOT `the claimant beat the tender by enough` `rejected $100,000 and recovered $120,000`
#ASSERT `the claimant pays the Registrar's costs` `rejected $100,000 and recovered $120,000`

-- $130,000 clears it.
#ASSERT `the claimant beat the tender by enough` `rejected $100,000 and recovered $130,000`
#ASSERT `the fund bears the claimant's costs` `rejected $100,000 and recovered $130,000`
#ASSERT NOT `the claimant pays the Registrar's costs` `rejected $100,000 and recovered $130,000`

#ASSERT `the claimant pays the Registrar's costs` `rejected $100,000 and recovered $90,000`

-- s 156(3) and (4): the only cost-free outcome is a final judgment that also
-- beats the tender by more than a fifth. Accepting the tender, and settling,
-- both leave the Registrar's costs with the claimant.
#ASSERT `the claimant pays the Registrar's costs` `accepted the tender`
#ASSERT `the fund bears the claimant's costs` `no tender, final judgment for $50,000`
#ASSERT `the claimant pays the Registrar's costs` `no tender, and the claim was settled`

§ `Sections 151(2) and 156(5) -- the thousand-dollar shortcut`

#ASSERT `section 156(5) lets the claimant go straight to the fund` 1000
#ASSERT NOT `section 156(5) lets the claimant go straight to the fund` 1001
#ASSERT `the Registrar may authorise payment without the Minister or the court` 1000
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may authorise payment without the Minister or the court` 1001

-- s 151(4): the fund running dry is not the claimant's problem.
#ASSERT `the deficiency is charged on and paid out of the Consolidated Fund` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the deficiency is charged on and paid out of the Consolidated Fund` FALSE

§ `Section 159 -- the second route to the fund, and the easier one`

GIVEN `corrected` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `dealt on the faith of it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `lost by the correction` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `years since` IS A NUMBER,
      `two or more titles` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Correction
DECIDE `a correction` `corrected` `dealt on the faith of it` `lost by the correction` `years since` `two or more titles` IS
    Correction WITH
        `the Registrar has exercised the power to correct the land-register` IS `corrected`
        `the claimant dealt on the faith of the erroneous registration` IS `dealt on the faith of it`
        `the claimant suffered loss or damage by the correction` IS `lost by the correction`
        `years since the deprivation occurred or the loss was sustained` IS `years since`
        `two or more titles are involved` IS `two or more titles`

`a boundary correction that cost the buyer land` MEANS `a correction` TRUE TRUE TRUE 2 FALSE
`a correction where the claimant never dealt on the register` MEANS `a correction` FALSE TRUE TRUE 2 FALSE
`a boundary correction, thirteen years on` MEANS `a correction` TRUE TRUE TRUE 13 FALSE
`a correction between two innocent proprietors` MEANS `a correction` TRUE TRUE TRUE 2 TRUE

#ASSERT `compensation is payable under section 159(5)` `a boundary correction that cost the buyer land`

-- s 159(5) asks for none of the three things s 155 asks for.
#ASSERT NOT `section 159(5) requires an omission, mistake or misfeasance of the Registrar`
#ASSERT NOT `section 159(5) requires the claimant to be barred from an action for recovery`
#ASSERT NOT `the section 155(3) exclusions apply to a section 159(5) claim`

-- SO THE BOUNDARY ERROR IS COMPENSABLE BY ONE ROUTE AND NOT THE OTHER. s 155(3)(b)
-- excludes it from the fund "under any circumstances"; s 159(2)(a) empowers the
-- Registrar to correct exactly that error; and s 159(5) compensates the person who
-- loses by the correction. The route runs through the Registrar choosing to
-- correct the register, and not otherwise.
#ASSERT `section 155(3) excludes compensation` `an incorrect description of the parcels, boundaries or dimensions from the Chief Surveyor`
#ASSERT NOT `an action against the assurance fund lies` `a boundary mis-description from the Chief Surveyor`
#ASSERT `compensation is payable under section 159(5)` `a boundary correction that cost the buyer land`

-- It needs the correction to have been made.
#ASSERT NOT `compensation is payable under section 159(5)` `a correction where the claimant never dealt on the register`

-- And it is subject to s 158's twelve years.
#ASSERT NOT `the claim is within the twelve years, for a section 159(5) claim` `a boundary correction, thirteen years on`
#ASSERT NOT `compensation is payable under section 159(5)` `a boundary correction, thirteen years on`

-- s 159(4): where two or more titles are involved, the tie-breaker between
-- innocent proprietors is the fund's exposure.
#ASSERT `the Registrar chooses between the titles by what it costs the fund` `a correction between two innocent proprietors`
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar chooses between the titles by what it costs the fund` `a boundary correction that cost the buyer land`

§ `Sections 152 and 153 -- the fund pays for these too`

#ASSERT `the applicant may summon the Registrar under section 152` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the applicant may summon the Registrar under section 152` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the applicant may summon the Registrar under section 152` FALSE TRUE

-- s 152(4): costs ordered against the Registrar come out of the assurance fund,
